  "style": {
    "name": "Vermilion Eaves — Cinnabar Way lacquered timber temple",
    "rationale": "Second pass: (1) broke every flat field — calcite panels are now recessed (omitted front course over a z1 backstop) and framed, each split by a raised red mullion; the podium gained deepslate pilaster strips and a red string-cap; (2) resolved columns into ENGAGED bays — six red posts bonded to the wall and projecting only as relief (z0-3), never freestanding, with a continuous red architrave beam tying them; (3) deepened relief — gold-capped tokyo bracket clusters step out under the eaves, and both jade roofs are terraced (4 stepped courses) with the lower eave overhanging the wall by 3 in z and past the body in x for a true shadow-line; (4) HELD the colorful complementary palette against the white reference — red_concrete dominant, prismarine_bricks jade roofs supporting, calcite neutral infill only, gold_block sparing on finials/brackets/lintel; (5) folded the pagoda spire into an engaged sorin crown seated on the upper ridge, not a detached tower; central bay widened to 1.4x side bays with a dark deepslate doorway niche under a gold lintel."
  },
